  "about": "One golden control request per desktop action. The frame the desktop sends for an action is {\"op\": \"control\", \"method\": <method>, \"params\": <params>}, the request the CLI's socket client writes (core/recursion_core/control/client.py). An action whose source is 'cli' is proven equal to the CLI's own request by desktop/tests/check_actions.py, against the CLI and against the frame the socket client actually writes. An action whose source is 'spine' takes its params from the named fixture of SPINE's draft schemas (pull request #368 at spine_head), and 'deltas' names every key in which the desktop's params differ from that fixture's and why; desktop/tests/sync_spine.py checks that against a checkout of that head. 'on_master' says whether the daemon at master_head answers the method; the others are table rows of a draft, not services.",
